Package: librescrs-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         liblibrescrs5 (>= 5.0),
         librescrs-card-plugins (>= 5.0),
         librescrs-pinentry-kde (= ${binary:Version}),
         p11-kit
Recommends: pcscd, policykit-1
Conflicts: librescrs-pkcs11-direct
Description: LibreSCRS smart-card session agent (D-Bus)
 A per-user, headless, Qt-free D-Bus session service that is the sole owner of
 smart-card access for the LibreSCRS stack. It works on any desktop.
 .
 Five of its files have to land in root-owned system directories -- a systemd
 user unit, two D-Bus drop-ins, a polkit action and a p11-kit registration --
 which is why no bundle format can deliver it and a distribution package is the
 only shape it can take.
 .
 The dependency on the prompter is hard rather than suggested. An agent with no
 prompter installs, activates over D-Bus, enumerates a card and then fails on
 the first PIN, because the interface it calls has no implementation.
 .
 The agent registers a PKCS#11 proxy with p11-kit, so it conflicts with
 librescrs-pkcs11-direct: one card must not have two providers and two security
 models.

Package: librescrs-pinentry-kde
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Secure PIN and CAN entry prompter for the LibreSCRS agent
 The prompter the agent calls to collect a PIN or a card access number. It is
 styled for KDE and built on KF6, and it is currently the only implementation
 of the prompter interface, so a GNOME or XFCE machine installs KF6::I18n and
 KF6::CoreAddons with it.
